  "abstract": "Covers the Arazzo Specification from the OpenAPI Initiative across its version lines: Arazzo 1.1 (current, 1.1.0), Arazzo 1.0 (supported, 1.0.1) and the Arazzo 1.2 draft on the v1.2-dev branch (preview, posture track, WSDL sources). It teaches source descriptions, workflows, steps, parameters, success criteria, success and failure actions, components and runtime expressions, AsyncAPI v3 send and receive steps, execution order and security for executors, validation against the official Arazzo JSON Schemas, and upgrading between lines. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, objects, expressions, AsyncAPI steps, execution, validation and examples.",
